{
	"Name": "AlertQuery - Okta - Policy - Rule - Okta Behavior Rule Fired POSITIVE",
	"Description": "A sign-on policy evaluation reported at least one behaviour rule as POSITIVE. Okta ThreatInsight behaviour rules flag a new device, a new IP, a new country, or impossible travel; a POSITIVE result means the sign-in did not look like this account's normal behaviour.\n\nThe behaviours arrive as a string map in debugContext.debugData.behaviors and, when the rules are in log-only mode, in debugContext.debugData.logOnlySecurityData.\n\nEvent type: policy.evaluate_sign_on\n\nReference(s):\n- https://help.okta.com/en-us/content/topics/security/behavior-detection/about-behavior-detection.htm\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/",
	"GUID": "6f184621-3dfd-51ff-a800-ffc14ed553d2",
